<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BTA '96 cons net falls to 15.6 bln esc.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BTA '96 cons net falls to 15.6 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to Dec 31:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Cons net 15.6 vs 17.2  </p>
<p>Financial margin 86.8 vs 86.1</p>
<p>Deposits 2,227.1 vs 2,060.4</p>
<p>Loans 1,545.0 vs 1,261.2</p>
<p>Net assets 3,514.8 vs 3,174.7</p>
<p>Cash flow 63.7 vs 65.3  </p>
<p>NOTE: Banco Totta e Acores is a Portuguese bank owned by businessman Antonio Champalimaud. BTA said its solvability ratio rose to 11.59 percent in 1996 from 11.22 percent in 1995.</p>
</text>
